        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "In ∆AOX and ΔAOY, we already know that AX = AY, and AO is common to both triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.128,
            0.611,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "If we can show that $\\angle XAO = \\angle YAO$ then, by the SAS congruence condition, we can conclude that the triangles are congruent."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.185,
            0.61,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "To show this, we observe that $\\Delta \\mathrm{ABX} \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm{ABY}.$ This is so because AX = AY, BX = BY, and AB is common to both the triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.243,
            0.611,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we have $\\angle \\mathrm{XAB} = \\angle \\mathrm{YAB},$ or $\\angle XAO = \\angle YAO$ because they are corresponding parts of congruent triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.628,
            0.138,
            0.918,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.299,
            0.595,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "Hence, AB is the perpendicular bisector of XY."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.33,
            0.52,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "We can have eyes of different shapes."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.408,
            0.474,
            0.438
          ],
